00:47:29,999 --> 00:47:35,999
The Transporter Refueled (French: Le Transporteur: Héritage; also known as Transporter 4) is a 2015 action
thriller film directed by Camille Delamarre and written by Bill Collage, Adam Cooper, and Luc Besson.

12
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:55,090
It serves as a reboot and the fourth film in the Transporter franchise.

13
00:56:08,181 --> 00:56:14,181
It stars Ed Skrein as Frank Martin, alongside Ray Stevenson, Loan Chabanol, Gabriella Wright, Tatjana
Pajković, Yu Wenxia, Radivoje Bukvić, Lenn Kudrjawizki, Anatole Taubman, and Noémie Lenoir.

14
01:00:27,272 --> 01:00:33,272
In the film, Frank finds himself caught up in a bank heist and
kidnapping plot orchestrated by Anna (Chabanol).

15
01:04:46,363 --> 01:04:52,363
A fourth Transporter film was planned to feature original franchise star Jason Statham, who was
offered a three film deal with EuropaCorp to produce additional installments.

16
01:09:05,454 --> 01:09:11,454
After negotiations with Statham fell through, Skrein was hired and the franchise was
rebooted, featuring no returning cast members from the first three films.

17
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
Principal photography took place in Paris.

18
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
The Transporter Refueled was theatrically released on 4 September 2015 in the United States and in France five
days later, by EuropaCorp; it is the first Transporter film primarily distributed by EuropaCorp.

19
01:22:02,727 --> 01:22:08,727
The film received negative reviews from critics and
grossed $72.6 million worldwide.

20
01:26:21,818 --> 01:26:27,818
The film explores themes of transporter, sequel,
french riviera, reboot, bank heist.

21
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The tone is intense.
